# Line endings.
#
# The tree is edited in NetBeans on Windows and from cloud sessions on Linux,
# and before this file it was a mix: about 120 files CRLF, 55 LF, each file
# keeping whichever it was born with. That costs every edit a check of the
# file's own ending and turns a one-line change into a whole-file diff the
# moment somebody's editor decides otherwise.
#
# The repository stores LF and checks out LF everywhere. NetBeans and javac
# do not mind; the batch files are the one thing Windows wants CRLF for.
#
# ONE-TIME STEP after this file lands, on the PC, in one commit of its own:
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "Normalise line endings to LF"
# Every CRLF file shows as modified in that commit and never again.

*               text=auto eol=lf
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.ico           binary
*.jar           binary
